## 1. Correcting the orbital synchronization

The existing viewer maps one complete Analemma traversal to only half of the inner circumference:

\[
\theta_{\rm orbit}=\frac{\phi_{\rm Analemma}}{2}
\]

That was inherited from the previous two-circuits-per-orbit gearing assumption. Your requirement is now clear: **one complete Analemma traversal must coincide with one complete revolution of the contact point around the inner circumference.**

So the relationship becomes:

\[
\boxed{\theta_{\rm orbit}=\phi_{\rm Analemma}}
\]

This applies to both curve settings. It also changes the corresponding provisional torus proportions:

